  <div id="lessonContent">
    <h2>1. What is DOM?</h2>
    <p><b>DOM = Document Object Model.</b> When your browser loads an HTML page, it converts the whole page into a tree of objects. That tree is called DOM.</p>
    <p>Example: Your HTML has <code>&lt;h1&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;p&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;button&gt;</code>. In DOM, each tag becomes an object. JavaScript can catch any object, read it, change it, delete it, or create a new one.</p>
    <div class="note"><b>Simple Meaning:</b> DOM is the bridge between HTML and JavaScript. Without DOM, JavaScript cannot touch HTML. With DOM, JavaScript can control the whole page.</div>
    <h2>2. LIVE DEMO - DOM Playground</h2>
    <p>Try all DOM powers on one box:</p>
    <div class="demo-card">
      <div id="domBox">
        <h3 id="domTitle" style="margin:0">I am a DOM Element 👋</h3>
        <p id="domPara" style="margin:8px 0">Change my text, color, size, hide me, or add new items.</p>
        <div id="domList"></div>
      </div>
      <button class="btn btn-js" onclick="domChangeText()">Change Text ✏️</button>
      <button class="btn btn-next" onclick="domChangeStyle()">Change Style 🎨</button>
      <button class="btn" onclick="domAddItem()">Add Item ➕</button>
      <button class="btn" onclick="domHide()">Hide / Show 👁️</button>
      <button class="btn" onclick="domReset()">Reset ↺</button>
    </div>
    <h2>3. How to Select an Element? - 4 Ways</h2>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Method</th><th>Selects</th><th>Example</th><th>Use When?</th></tr>
      <tr><td><b>getElementById("id")</b></td><td>One element by id</td><td>getElementById("title")</td><td>Most used - When you have id</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>querySelector(".class")</b></td><td>First match</td><td>querySelector(".box")</td><td>Modern way - CSS selector</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>querySelectorAll("p")</b></td><td>All matches</td><td>querySelectorAll("p")</td><td>When you need all items</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>getElementsByClassName</b></td><td>All with same class</td><td>getElementsByClassName("card")</td><td>Old way, still works</td></tr>
    </table>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">// 1. By ID - Returns ONE element</span><br>
<span class="text">let title = document.getElementById("title");</span><br><br>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">// 2. By CSS Selector - Returns FIRST match</span><br>
<span class="text">let firstBox = document.querySelector(".box");</span><br>
<span class="text">let firstPara = document.querySelector("p");</span><br>
<span class="text">let byId = document.querySelector("#title"); // Same as getElementById</span><br><br>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">// 3. All - Returns a LIST, use loop</span><br>
<span class="text">let allParas = document.querySelectorAll("p");</span><br>
<span class="text">console.log(allParas.length); // How many p tags?</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>4. Change Text - innerHTML vs textContent</h2>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Property</th><th>What It Does</th><th>Example</th></tr>
      <tr><td><b>innerHTML</b></td><td>Change text + HTML tags inside</td><td>el.innerHTML = "&lt;b&gt;Bold&lt;/b&gt;" - Shows BOLD</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>textContent</b></td><td>Change only plain text, tags show as text</td><td>el.textContent = "&lt;b&gt;Bold&lt;/b&gt;" - Shows &lt;b&gt;Bold&lt;/b&gt;</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>innerText</b></td><td>Same as textContent, but respects CSS hidden</td><td>el.innerText = "Hello"</td></tr>
    </table>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="text">let h = document.getElementById("title");</span><br>
<span class="text">h.innerHTML = "Hello &lt;b&gt;Ali&lt;/b&gt;"; // Shows: Hello Ali (Ali bold)</span><br>
<span class="text">h.textContent = "Hello &lt;b&gt;Ali&lt;/b&gt;"; // Shows: Hello &lt;b&gt;Ali&lt;/b&gt; (as text)</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="note"><b>Rule:</b> If you want to add HTML tags like &lt;b&gt;, &lt;br&gt;, &lt;img&gt;, use <b>innerHTML</b>. If you only want plain text from user input (safe), use <b>textContent</b>.</div>
    <h2>5. Change Style From JavaScript</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="text">let box = document.getElementById("myBox");</span><br><br>
<span class="text">box.style.color = "red"; // Text color</span><br>
<span class="text">box.style.backgroundColor = "yellow"; // NOTE: background-color becomes backgroundColor</span><br>
<span class="text">box.style.fontSize = "30px";</span><br>
<span class="text">box.style.display = "none"; // Hide element</span><br>
<span class="text">box.style.display = "block"; // Show again</span>
    </code></div>
    <p><b>Important:</b> In CSS we write <code>background-color</code>. In JS we write <code>backgroundColor</code> - Remove dash, make next letter capital. This is called <b>camelCase</b>.</p>
    <h2>6. Change Attributes - src, href, value</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">// Change Image</span><br>
<span class="text">document.getElementById("myImg").src = "new-photo.jpg";</span><br><br>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">// Change Link</span><br>
<span class="text">document.getElementById("myLink").href = "https://google.com";</span><br><br>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">// Get / Set Input Value</span><br>
<span class="text">let name = document.getElementById("nameInput").value; // READ</span><br>
<span class="text">document.getElementById("nameInput").value = "Ali"; // WRITE</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>7. Create and Delete Elements</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">// CREATE - Make new p tag and add to page</span><br>
<span class="text">let newPara = document.createElement("p");</span><br>
<span class="text">newPara.textContent = "I am a new paragraph!";</span><br>
<span class="text">document.getElementById("container").appendChild(newPara);</span><br><br>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">// DELETE - Remove element from page</span><br>
<span class="text">let old = document.getElementById("oldItem");</span><br>
<span class="text">old.remove();</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>8. Complete Example - Dark Mode Toggle</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;html&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;body</span> <span class="attr">id</span>=<span class="val">"page"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><br><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;h1</span> <span class="attr">id</span>=<span class="val">"title"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text">My Website</span><span class="tag">&lt;/h1&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;button</span> <span class="attr">onclick</span>=<span class="val">"toggleDark()"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text">Dark Mode 🌙</span><span class="tag">&lt;/button&gt;</span><br><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;script&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let isDark = false;</span><br><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">function toggleDark() {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let page = document.getElementById("page");</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let title = document.getElementById("title");</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">if (isDark === false) {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">page.style.backgroundColor = "#0f172a";</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">title.style.color = "white";</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">isDark = true;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">} else {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">page.style.backgroundColor = "white";</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">title.style.color = "black";</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">isDark = false;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">}</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">}</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;/script&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;/body&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;/html&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>9. Homework</h2>
    <p>In Playground, build this:</p>
    <p>1. One h1 and 3 buttons - Red, Green, Blue. On click, change h1 color with <code>.style.color</code><br>2. One input + button - On click, take input value and show it in h1 with <code>innerHTML</code><br>3. Dark Mode toggle like the example above - One button changes full page background</p>
    <div class="box"><b>Remember:</b> DOM = Page as objects tree | document = Whole page | getElementById = Select by id | querySelector = Select by CSS selector | innerHTML = Change text + HTML | textContent = Plain text only | .style.color = Change CSS from JS | background-color in CSS = backgroundColor in JS | createElement + appendChild = Create new | .remove() = Delete | .value = Input value</div>
    <p><b>Next Step:</b> <a href="/lesson31">Lesson 31 - Events</a> - Learn click, mouse, keyboard, input events. Make your page respond to everything.</p>
